.TH AVR\-SETTINGS\-LIST 1 "" "avr 0.1.6" "Avrea CLI"
.SH NAME
avr-settings-list \- List settings with their current values and source.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B avr settings list
[OPTIONS]
.SH DESCRIPTION
List settings with their current values and source.
.PP
Inside a connected checkout the repository is auto-detected from the git remote and its effective values are shown. Pass --org to see organization values (this suppresses auto-detection), or --repo / AVR_REPO to target a repository.
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
Examples:
    avr settings list --org org-abc123
    avr settings list --org org-abc123 --repo rep-xyz789
    avr settings list --repo acme/web
    avr settings list --prefix cache.
    avr settings list --json key,value,source
.fi
.RE
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
JSON FIELDS
    key, source, value
.fi
.RE
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-org\fR \fITEXT\fR
Organization ID or slug. Uses default org if not specified.
.TP
\fB\-\-repo\fR \fITEXT\fR
Repository (org/repo or rep-xxx). Auto-detected from git unless --org given.
.TP
\fB\-\-prefix\fR \fITEXT\fR
Filter by key prefix (e.g. 'cache.').
.TP
\fB\-\-web\fR
Open in browser.
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR \fITEXT\fR
Output JSON. Pass comma-separated field names, "*" for all fields, or "?" to list available fields.
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-jq\fR \fITEXT\fR
Filter --json output through a jq expression.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR avr (1),
.BR avr-settings (1),
.BR avr-settings-reset (1),
.BR avr-settings-schema (1),
.BR avr-settings-set (1)
